            "review_title": "Review at Lang Nuong Nam Bo",
            "review_text": "LamN\nSingapore, Singapore4905 contributions\n2\nImmensely popular with the local middle class\nAug 2018 • Family\nLàng Nướng Nam Bộ specialises in roasted suckling pig and grilled meats (boar, deer, rabbit, chicken, duck, etc), but also dishes that originate from and are popular in southern Vietnam (hotpot of various kinds). Although there is a menu in English and you may be able to find an English-speaking staff member, the clientele is over 90% local, with the rest being mainly overseas Vietnamese. The restaurant is so successful (it’s often full even on weeknights) that it expanded recently to this gigantic location, in addition to having several branches. Prices are very reasonable. The food is not the best, but quite good. Even with hundreds of customers, service is extremely attentive and efficient; they constantly change the ice in your beer mugs to keep it cold. A great place to watch how ordinary middle-class Vietnamese enjoy themselves. They consume an enormous amount of beer, easily 5-10 per person from the amount of empty cans and bottles besides each table (for billing purposes).\nRead more\nWritten August 22, 2018",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-14",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
