            "review_title": "Review at Lang Nuong Nam Bo",
            "review_text": "JoUET11\nSaratoga, California195 contributions\n0\nVery Popular & Festive\nJan 2018 • Family\nWe dined here on a Friday evening with relatives who are locals. This is a huge restaurant filled with perhaps three hundred people. It was very noisy with music and mostly people in their twenties. The waiters were dressed in outfits that look like they came from Robin Hood story book. The food is relatively inexpensive and tasty. The menu has an extensive offering of different meats. We had deer and rabbit meat grilled at our table. Diners also have option of having meat dishes pre-grilled in the kitchen. Our favorite is the coconut salad and grilled scallops.\nRead more\nWritten January 12, 2018",
